From 1a8e90483c6d6559f57ff9a2c1688d5657e45e66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:42:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: frame start pacing counts a busy GPU as spare time; pass
 shape and present step timing

In busy scenes the GPU is still on the frame before when the game calls
Present(), so the new frame's command lists wait for the GPU anyway. The
spare time formula assumed the GPU starts a frame as soon as the game hands
it over, found no spare time in fights and held nothing back, so fights
showed about 80 ms from frame start to screen. A frame that reaches Present()
while the GPU is busy now counts that wait as spare time, capped by the room
its present has before it would be late.

Diagnostics: the pass meter measures the shape of the costliest passes
(when the last screen tile began, CPU vertex counts, sampled pipeline
statistics, pipeline binds; VKD3D_FEX_PASS_SHAPE=0 turns it off), and the
present timeline times the fence wait flush, the VkQueue lock wait and the
work after vkQueuePresentKHR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WLFWPd69Fe8cXrKbfompEp
